    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3971D0B7A1DB06DA25282DE787EC51E9/jobs/264212": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach - Swimming & Diving PT",
      "description": "Assistant Coach - Swimming & Diving PT You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Coach - Swimming & Diving PT Midland University - Fremont, NE 68025 Apply Apply Description Part-Time Assistant Swimming & Diving Coach Midland University, a private liberal arts university located in Fremont, Nebraska, just outside the Omaha metropolitan area, is seeking a Part-Time Assistant Swimming & Diving Coach to join the Midland University Swimming & Diving program. The successful candidate will work closely with the Head Coach and be involved in all aspects of the program, including coaching, athlete development, recruiting, practice preparation, team travel, and program administration. This position is a great opportunity for someone looking to develop as a collegiate coach while gaining hands-on experience within a growing and nationally competitive NAIA swimming program . The assistant coach will have opportunities to work directly with student-athletes, contribute to training and program development, gain recruiting experience, and take on additional responsibilities as they grow within the role. Job Responsibilities Assist with coaching and instruction during practices and competitions Work with the Head Coach to create and implement training programs for different swimming groups Provide technical instruction and feedback to student-athletes Assist with recruiting and retention of prospective student-athletes Build relationships and communicate with prospective athletes and their families through phone, text, email, video calls, and in-person meetings Assist with practice preparation, scheduling, team administration, and day-to-day program operations Travel with the team to away competitions and assist with team transportation Contribute to the continued growth and success of Midland's nationally competitive men's and women's swimming programs Help create a positive team environment focused on athlete development, accountability, and the student-athlete experience Maintain personal conduct and program standards consistent with Midland University's mission and core values Potential opportunity to coach with the Fremont Area Swim Team (FAST) during the summer season, contingent upon FAST approval Perform additional duties as assigned by the Head Coach What This Position Offers This position provides an opportunity to gain meaningful experience in collegiate coaching, recruiting, athlete development, and program operations while working directly with a growing roster of student-athletes. The assistant coach will have the opportunity to contribute ideas, develop as a coach, take ownership of responsibilities within the program, and play an important role in the continued growth of Midland Swimming & Diving. For someone interested in building a career in collegiate swimming, this position provides valuable hands-on experience across both the coaching and recruiting sides of a college program . Compensation Monthly stipend Potential additional summer coaching opportunities. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Minimum of 2–4 years of collegiate swimming experience as a coach and/or student-athlete Strong understanding of swimming technique, training principles, and athlete development Familiarity with collegiate and USA Swimming rules Strong communication and relationship-building skills Positive attitude, reliability, initiative, and willingness to learn Ability to work independently while also contributing as part of a coaching staff Ability to work a flexible schedule, including early mornings, evenings, weekends, team travel, and recruiting USA Swimming non-athlete membership, or ability to obtain Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree Previous swimming coaching experience USA Swimming coaching certification National-level swimming experience Experience recruiting high school and/or collegiate student-athletes Previous experience within a collegiate swimming program CDL with passenger and air brake endorsements, or willingness to obtain Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
