    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3971D0B7A1DB06DA25282DE787EC51E9/jobs/264136": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Nursing You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant/Associate Professor - Nursing Midland University - Fremont, NE 68025 Apply Apply Description Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing (Mental Health Instructor) - School of Nursing Midland University, a private liberal-arts college in Fremont, Nebraska, (just outside of metro Omaha) is seeking an exceptional nursing faculty member with expertise in mental health for a full-time position in the School of Nursing beginning August 2027. Responsibilities will include but not be limited to: ● Teaching course and clinical content to include didactic, clinical and simulation ● Creating engaging and innovative learning experiences that foster clinical judgment, critical thinking, professional development, and the application of evidence-based nursing practice ● Mentoring students to promote academic success and professional growth ● Participation in student recruitment and retention efforts ● Outcome assessment and data collection to ensure continuous improvement and to meet regulator and accreditation requirements ● Serving on departmental and university committees that support the Mission of Midland University and the School of Nursing ● Supporting accreditation, regulatory, and State Board requirements and initiatives Qualifications Qualifications: ● Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse License in the state of Nebraska, or eligibility and ability to obtain Nebraska licensure by endorsement ● Master of Science in Nursing (MSN), doctoral degree preferred ● Minimum of 2 years’ professional nursing experience, preferably in mental health/psychiatric nursing. ● Ability to meet clinical agency requirements, such as a background check, abuse check, drug testing, CPR, immunizations, health care insurance, and etc. ● Passion for preparing nursing professionals with the knowledge and skills to enter the health care marketplace. ● Ability to create relevant learning opportunities in the class and clinical setting that meet professional expectations and standards. ● Commitment to fostering an inclusive environment for faculty, staff, and students. The ideal candidate will possess the following: ● Previous teaching experience in nursing education. ● Familiarity with Canvas or other Learning Management System that facilitates face to face, hybrid, and online teaching modalities. ● Strong interpersonal, communication, and collaboration skills. ● The ability to foster a positive work culture that encourages change and innovation. ● The ability to interact effectively with internal and external stakeholders. Applicants should complete the online application and upload both a resume and a cover letter that highlights their qualifications, teaching philosophy, and interest in joining the School of Nursing at Midland University. Compensation/Benefits: ● Salary commensurate with education, experience, and individual strengths ● An engaging, respectful and productive working environment ● Access to campus events, including sporting events and theatrical performances. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3971D0B7A1DB06DA25282DE787EC51E9/jobs/262483": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Supply Chain Management",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Supply Chain Management You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Supply Chain Management Midland University - Fremont, NE 68025 Start Date   09/04/2026 Apply Apply Description Midland University, a private, Christian, liberal-arts college in Fremont, Nebraska, is seeking exceptional faculty members to teach Supply Chain Management in our undergraduate business program. The class will run in-person (no online option available) during the Fall session 2027: January 11-May 7. The hybrid class is scheduled for Mondays and Wednesdays from 8-8:50 am. In this course, the learner will be exposed to the basic principles of supply chain management including an integrated view of procurement, manufacturing and operations management, transportation and logistics, inventory and warehousing, demand planning, scheduling, network design, collaboration, and performance management. Learners will also explore financial metrics and decision support tools commonly used in managing supply chains. Professionals with extensive practical experience and an interest in engaging students are encouraged to apply, regardless of previous classroom experience. Applications for this position will be accepted until the position is filled. Cover letters are strongly encouraged. Qualifications Need to have: Master’s degree in business-related field Experience in supply chain Should demonstrate: Interest and experience engaging students through classroom learning The desire and availability to be quickly responsive to students Nice to have: Experience working with a learning management system such as Blackboard or Canvas to develop and deliver course content Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3971D0B7A1DB06DA25282DE787EC51E9/jobs/260906": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Student Teacher Supervisor",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Student Teacher Supervisor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Student Teacher Supervisor Midland University - Fremont, NE 68025 Start Date   08/26/2026 Apply Apply Description Midland University, a private, faith-based, liberal arts university in Fremont, Nebraska (just outside of metro Omaha), is seeking multiple Student Teacher Supervisors to support the Three to Teach and Teacher Career Ladder programs. Student Teacher Supervisor School: Walker School of Education Position type: Part-time adjunct Location: Nebraska—localized assignments within the supervisor’s district or surrounding areas Term: Spring 2027 Application deadline: Open until all positions are filled. Position Overview The Walker School of Education at Midland University seeks experienced educators throughout Nebraska to serve as clinical practice/student teacher supervisors for paraeducators completing the student-teaching or clinical-practice term of their teacher- preparation program. These teacher candidates are practicing paraeducators who are beginning the student- teaching portion of their program. Supervisors will support candidates throughout their clinical experience through classroom observations, conferences, feedback, documentation, and collaboration with mentor teachers and university personnel. Supervisors will generally be assigned to candidates in their own school district or in neighboring districts. Assignments are intended to involve a reasonable commute within the supervisor’s local area and surrounding communities; extensive statewide travel is not expected. Essential Responsibilities ● Conduct scheduled classroom observations of assigned teacher candidates. ● Provide timely, specific, and constructive feedback on teaching performance. ● Support candidates in lesson planning, instruction, classroom management, assessment, and professional practice. ● Collaborate with school-based cooperating teachers and appropriate school personnel. ● Participate in conferences with the teacher candidate and cooperating teacher. ● Review lesson plans, teaching artifacts, required assignments, and portfolio materials. ● Complete observation reports, evaluations, and other required documentation. ● Communicate regularly with the university coordinator regarding candidate progress. ● Identify strengths, concerns, and areas for professional growth. ● Address concerns promptly and participate in improvement planning when necessary. ● Attend required supervisor orientation, training, and professional-development activities. ●Maintain confidentiality and comply with university, school-district, and professional requirements. Time Commitment The assignment and workload will vary based on the number and location of assigned candidates. Supervisors should anticipate responsibilities that may include: ● Approximately 1-4 teacher candidates per term ● Five required formal observations per candidate ● Pre- and post-observation conferences ● Communication with candidates, Cooperating Teachers, and university personnel ● Completion of online evaluations and documentation ● Participation in required meetings or training ●Most observations and conferences will occur during the school day and will be scheduled in collaboration with the candidate and school personnel. Geographic Expectations Student teacher supervisors are needed throughout Nebraska. Supervisors will typically be assigned to paraeducators completing their clinical practice in: ● Their own school district ● Neighboring school districts ● Nearby communities within a reasonable commuting distance ●Supervisors must have reliable transportation and be able to travel to assigned school sites. Compensation Compensation will be discussed with candidates who are selected for the position. Compensation is generally based on the number of teacher candidates supervised. Qualifications Required Qualifications ● Master’s degree in education or a related field. ● Valid Nebraska teaching certificate or equivalent state-issued teaching credential. ● At least five years of successful classroom teaching experience. ● Experience working with students at grade levels or in subject areas relevant to assigned candidates. ● Strong communication, observation, organization, and interpersonal skills. ● Ability to provide professional, specific, and constructive feedback. ● Reliable transportation for travel to assigned school sites. ● Ability to use email, online meeting platforms, and digital evaluation systems. Preferred Qualifications ● Experience mentoring, coaching, supervising, or evaluating teachers or teacher candidates. ● Experience working with paraeducators or nontraditional teacher candidates. ● Experience supporting adult learners. ● Knowledge of teacher-preparation clinical-practice requirements. ● Experience with observation rubrics, professional portfolios, or teacher-evaluation systems. ● School leadership, instructional-coaching, or administrative experience. ● Elementary, secondary, special education, or other licensure relevant to assigned candidates. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3971D0B7A1DB06DA25282DE787EC51E9/jobs/257041": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Tennis",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant - Tennis You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Graduate Assistant - Tennis Midland University - Fremont, NE 68025 Start Date   08/07/2026 Apply Apply Description Midland University, a private liberal arts university in Fremont, Nebraska (just outside of metro Omaha), is seeking a Graduate Assistant - Men's and Women's Tennis Coach. The coaching position will be offered within our graduate assistant structure, requiring admission to the University's Master of Education, Master of Science Learning and Talent Development, Master of Science and Sports Administration and Leadership, or Master of Business Administration programs. In addition to the academic responsibilities, the candidate will be responsible for contributing to various aspects of the tennis program, including assistant coaching, program administration, practice preparation, and other duties assigned by the Head Coach. The person who holds this position will receive tuition remission from the University and potentially receive a campus meal plan and monthly stipend. Job responsibilities include: Representing Midland University Assisting the head coach with the administration and leadership of the tennis program Providing coaching and instruction during training and practice activities Recruiting Practice preparation Overseeing team travel Directing strength and conditioning activities during the season and off-season Video analysis Scheduling Equipment management Running camps and clinics Helping to ensure team compliance with all NAIA and institutional rules and regulations Need to have: A bachelor's degree Must meet eligibility for Midland University Graduate Program Valid CDL License (or can obtain one shortly after starting in this role) Previous tennis coaching experience Ability to effectively coordinate recruiting events Strong organizational and interpersonal communication skills Basic computer skills, such as a working understanding of Microsoft Word and Excel Should demonstrate: A positive attitude An ability to resolve issues independently Compensation: Tuition Remission in the master's program. Level of remission is dependent on degree pursued Free campus meal plan (15 meals per week) Monthly stipend dependent on degree pursued Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3971D0B7A1DB06DA25282DE787EC51E9/jobs/256905": {
      "title": "Assistant Track and Field Coach",
